  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal word that appears almost exclusively in news reports, police records, and legal documents. In everyday speech, {殴|なぐ}る (to punch) or {叩|たた}く (to hit) are used instead. Often seen in crime reporting alongside terms like {傷害|しょうがい} (injury/assault).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {殴打|おうだ}する (to strike, to beat)\n- {殴打|おうだ}による{死亡|しぼう} (death by beating)\n- {頭部|とうぶ}を{殴打|おうだ}する (to strike on the head)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {殴|なぐ}る: to punch, to hit — everyday word for striking someone\n- {暴行|ぼうこう}: assault, violence — broader legal term covering various types of physical attack",
